WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
Follow four synthetic parts through a query and supplier join. The part names come from the quick start. Dimensions are illustrative.

2
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.500
A part ID identifies a part. A supplier ID connects it to a supplier. The executable join uses the supplier relationship.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.250
Select parts 1, 2 and 3. Leave the bracket outside the result. The example reads the file before temporary storage is removed.

4
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:15.000
Bolt and washer reach Supplier B. Nut reaches Supplier A. The animation follows the saved quick-start output.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.750
A missing value must remain an explicit filter in the query. Rows 2 and 4 contain 10 and 20; they stay outside the result.

6
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.500
A real local ClickHouse checks the rows returned by the patch. Contributor verification is separate from upstream acceptance.

7
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.250
Exercise installed wheels outside the source checkout. The supported minimum is a maintainer-review proposal.

8
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.000
Explore the scene, executable example and focused contributions. No Neuralink affiliation or adoption is implied.
